        "arguments": "{\"code\":\"import os, sys, json\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nroot = Path(r'C:\\\\Users\\\\12159\\\\Desktop\\\\ai_exec\\\\responses')\\nsys.path.insert(0, str(root))\\nfrom skills.context_compaction.compact import compact_active_file\\nsummary = r'''# Compacted context summary\\n\\n## Active goal\\nPolish and maintain the multi-conversation UX in the three ai_exec viewers while keeping context manageable. Do not revisit settled rail UX unless requested.\\n\\n## Workspace and launch\\n- Root: C:\\\\Users\\\\12159\\\\Desktop\\\\ai_exec\\n- Active viewer/cwd: responses/viewer.py\\n- Other equivalent viewers: chat_completions/viewer.py, messages/viewer.py\\n- Launch: ./view.vbs -> pythonw viewer.py\\n- Active transcript: responses/input.json; named chats use input_对话名.json\\n- Active pointer: .ae_active_input\\n- Context skill: responses/skills/context_compaction; use it for future compactions.\\n\\n## Architecture/features already completed\\n- Markdown rendering uses inlined marked 11.1.1 and DOMPurify 3.1.6.\\n- Code blocks use highlight.js 11.9.0 CDN and enhanceCodeBlocks().\\n- Multi-chat APIs: list/create/select/rename/delete; default chat protected.\\n- New chats auto-name 新对话 / 新对话2... and copy default config with transcript cleared.\\n- Active chat persists through .ae_active_input.\\n- Settled chat rail: fixed top-left, transparent/no frame/avatar/collapse, only '+' create control, adaptive width and main-content padding, hides metadata/search at narrow widths and leaves only '+' at very narrow widths.\\n\\n## Latest request and work\\nUser asked to read complete viewer.py and inspect bugs. responses/viewer.py was read in full (then 2077 lines). Fixes were applied identically to all three viewer.py files:\\n1. Call _restore_active_input() during startup; it was previously defined but unused.\\n2. Harden chat IDs/path handling to reject traversal/invalid IDs.\\n3. Make state cache file-aware using active path + mtime_ns + size; prevent a threaded old-chat read from populating the new-chat cache.\\n4. Add usage request generation/queue guards so stale /api/usage responses cannot overwrite the newly selected chat.\\n5. Queue chat-list reloads instead of dropping loadChats() requests while one is active.\\n6. Deleting an inactive chat no longer clears the current draft/transcript UI; reset only if active chat changes.\\n7. Backend /api/chats/select now returns 400 for invalid IDs.\\n\\nModified files:\\n- responses/viewer.py\\n- chat_completions/viewer.py\\n- messages/viewer.py\\n\\n## Verification\\n- Python compile passed for all three viewers.\\n- Every inline JavaScript block passed `node --check` in all three viewers.\\n- Backend temporary-directory tests passed for all API variants: active restore, traversal rejection, create/clear, rename, delete, and cache separation between same-size/same-mtime chat files.\\n- Browser integration was attempted with Python Playwright but not run because its bundled Chromium was not installed. Microsoft Edge exists, but user said waiting was too long, so no further browser automation/download was pursued.\\n- The currently open viewer process may still be running pre-fix code; restart via view.vbs to load edits.\\n\\n## Wheel/reuse assessment\\n- Third-party reuse is reasonable: marked, DOMPurify, highlight.js; backend remains Python-standard-library-only.\\n- Internal reuse is poor: 93.4%-96.2% of nonblank lines are exactly shared across the three viewers.\\n- Approx responses/viewer.py after fixes: 158 KB / 2168 lines; PAGE ~122 KB; marked 35 KB; DOMPurify 21 KB; app JS 41 KB; CSS 20 KB.\\n- Best future refactor: extract shared backend/page/assets and keep three thin API adapters for transcript conversion, append/retract, and clear operations. Do not begin this refactor unless the user asks.\\n\\n## Exact next task\\nContext compaction was requested and is now being performed. Afterward, wait for the user's next request. If asked to continue code work, prefer targeted checks and avoid long browser/download steps unless explicitly requested.'''\\nresult = compact_active_file(input_path=root / 'input.json', summary=summary)\\nprint(json.dumps(result, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))\"}"
